Declare what each variable is: required, format, secret.

Writes `[vars.*]` into `.evnx.toml` — the contract `.env.example` cannot express. A project with no spec behaves exactly as it does today.

Usage: evnx spec [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init   Generate a first spec from this project, or from named components
  check  Check the contract against `.env.example`, and `.env` when there is one. Read-only; suited to a pre-commit hook and to CI
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --no-color
          Disable colored output

  -q, --quiet
          Print nothing on success. Findings, warnings, errors and requested data still print

  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose output

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Full guide: https://docs.evnx.dev/cli/commands/spec
